Fix round complete. Applied all 2 P1s, both P2s, and all 5 P3s from the reviewer's findings:

- **P1-1** (`:str` bypassed UTF-16 guard): routed through `encode-scalar` in `encode-operand`, and tightened the structural `:str` kind check so `image-defect` catches it too.
- **P1-2** (scope validator dropped conflicting chains): `walk-body`/`all-body-chains` now detect a body pc reached with a different chain and report `:scope-conflict`; verified with the reviewer's fixture in both declaration orders.
- **P2-1** (JVM BigDecimal/Float silently folded): `host-double?` now requires `(instance? Double v)` on JVM.
- **P2-2** (no refusal-path test existed): added a cross-host lone-surrogate deftest covering all four throw sites.
- **P3-1..P3-5**: added `[:ffi-call 2]` to saturation, qualified the ratio-out-of-range refusal, bounded `:uint`/`:pc` to safe-integer on CLJS, moved prose out of the hashed descriptor, and widened `image-scalar-classes` to scan every `:data` operand.

Testing: 16 deftests/132 assertions on the new test namespace, full JVM suite (1727 tests/172682 assertions) and full CLJS suite via shadow-cljs (1644 tests/42505 assertions, 0 warnings) both clean. kondo, cljstyle, and the CLJD lane were denied by the permission system and not retried — the CLJD branch of the new surrogate fixture is consequently unverified, flagged explicitly in the report.

One expected side effect: P3-4 (removing hashed prose from the descriptor) forked `descriptor-hash`, so all four golden `image-hash` pins changed — `encode-image` bytes themselves didn't. This is called out explicitly per the "stop and report why" instruction rather than changed silently.

Full details are in `collab/1790061302828-yinvm-engineer-debruijn-b1-fix.claude-sonnet-5.stdout.log`, including one open item flagged for the reviewer: P2-1 has no dedicated pinned-literal test (verified manually instead, reusing P2-2's mechanism test).
